----|---|-------|------|------|\n\n**#794** 8:42 PM 🔵 **Gateway `hooks.internal` Configuration Schema**\n\nThe primary session queried the gateway configuration schema for the `hooks.internal` path. This path governs trusted in-process automations — internal event handlers loaded from module paths. The schema is strict (`additionalProperties: false`) and all fields are optional but tagged as `advanced`. The `load` sub-key controls where handler modules are discovered at startup, while `entries` registers concrete runtime handlers. The system design emphasizes auditability: handler definitions should be explicit, entries versioned, and load roots constrained to avoid module conflicts. This was likely explored in the context of the user's earlier request to update a GPT model setting — possibly investigating whether model routing or selection is handled via internal hooks.\n\nRead: ~422\n\n**#S271** User asked about GPT model update + system responded with current hook configuration status (Mar 9, 8:44 PM)\n\n**General**\n| ID | Time | T | Title | Read | Work |\n|----|------|---|-------|------|------|\n\n**#795** 8:48 PM 🔵 **OpenClaw Session Running on GPT-5.3-Codex Model**\n\nThe OpenClaw agent session status was checked in response to the user's request to upgrade the active GPT model. The system is currently running on openai-codex/gpt-5.3-codex. The user observed that a newer GPT model has been released and asked for the model to be changed to a higher/newer version. This check establishes the baseline model configuration before any potential upgrade.\n\nRead: ~236\n\n**~/.openclaw/openclaw.json**\n| ID | Time | T | Title | Read | Work |\n|----|------|---|-------|------|------|\n\n**#796** \" 🔵 **OpenClaw Config Already Set to GPT-5.4 as Default Model**\n\nAfter the user requested upgrading to a newer GPT model, the model configuration was inspected. The config already lists \"openai-codex/gpt-5.4\" as the default model, yet the active session is running on \"openai-codex/gpt-5.3-codex\" (the fallback). This suggests the session started before gpt-5.4 was fully available or the fallback was triggered for another reason. The current session is not using the intended default model despite the config being up to date.\n\nRead: ~291\n\n\nAccess 131k tokens of past research & decisions for just 16,706t. Use the claude-mem skill to access memories by ID."}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773056982274}}
